  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting inclusive civic participation, violence free, fair and peaceful election</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is initiated to harnessed collaboration among three partners with long lasting work on the democratic and electoral processes in Sierra Leone. The proposed project will specifically target Port Loko, Kambia, Karene, Bombali, Kailahun, Kenema, Kono, Western Area Urban &amp; Rural whiles the other districts will also benefit from few of the project activities. These districts were deliberately selected on the bases that they are mainly associated as hotspot districts and decline of women&#x2019;s participation in the electoral process from all bye-elections conducted since the 2018 General Election. This project is complementing the efforts of the Electoral Commission of Sierra Leone (ECSL) charged with the legal responsibility to run the affairs of state elections and synergy of efforts with other state actors contributing to the democratic and electoral process in Sierra Leone. 
In the recent national voters&#x2019; registration conducted across the country, IRCSL, 50/50 Group and FVMC significantly contributed to the registration process by raising mass national awareness using diverse modes to commit voters&#x2019; interests to register. This proposed project aligns with CAFOD&#x2019;s integral ecology model that build the connections and relationships needed for healthy, flourishing communities and environments embedded with community well-being, including conflict prevention and resolution, justice and peace and broader civic issues. The IRCSL will be the lead implementing partner and bears the primary responsibility of accountability to CAFOD. The IRCSL had been supported by CAFOD to contribute to the democratic and electoral processes, environmental sustainability, national cohesion, peacebuilding, COVID-19 awareness raising, humanitarian response and capacity building support.</narrative>
  </description>
